 "DEFECT": "DEFECT-QBTGT: each position's depth table is measured on one field (QB on pass attempts, RB on carries, WR/TE on targets) and allocate_opportunity read its share as the prior for EVERY field, so a quarterback's 0.95 pass-attempt share became his target prior. Deshaun Watson carried 5.04 projected targets on 2026-10-01; nine of sixty main-slate quarterbacks carried 4.4-5.7. The simulator gives quarterbacks no target share, so those targets reached nobody in any joint world.",
 "ARMS": {
  "LEGACY": "LEGACY_CROSS_FIELD_PRIOR=True, the pre-2026-10-02 allocator",
  "QB_ONLY": "CROSS_FIELD_PRIOR_SCOPE=QB_ONLY: quarterback rows take group split x within-group concentration for targets and carries; other positions unchanged. PRODUCTION DEFAULT.",
  "ALL": "CROSS_FIELD_PRIOR_SCOPE=ALL: every cross-field case repaired (backs' targets, receivers' carries too). CANDIDATE ARM, not promoted."
 },
 "DESIGN": "forward_chain.evaluate on seasons 2024,2025 with the panel at HEAD: 28 held-out weeks, identical across the three runs (asserted), the same six blend arms. Differences are paired by week with a week-blocked SE. This is EXPLORATORY: the forward chain is development data that already chose constants and arms; it establishes direction and size, not a confirmatory result.",
 "READING": "Quarterback error is unchanged under either scope (within 0.005 DK points). Receiver, tight end and back MAE rise by 0.05-0.25 while their level ratio (mean projection / mean actual) rises from about 0.70-0.79 toward 0.78-0.88. Removing the ghost targets scales every other receiver on the club up by roughly a fifth: the level moves toward honest, the ranking is flat, the absolute error rises. The legacy ghost was therefore acting as an undeclared shrinkage on receiver projections -- a fitted constant by accident. The quarterback repair stands as a proven football contradiction; the receiver mass it exposed (projection on rows that do not score) is the next defect, recorded here rather than hidden by keeping an impossible allocation.",
